#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:3
msgid "How to Migrate from VS Code to Zed"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:5
msgid ""
"This guide explains how to move from VS Code to Zed without rebuilding your "
"workflow."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:7
msgid ""
"It covers which settings import automatically, which shortcuts map cleanly, "
"and which behaviors differ so you can adjust quickly."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:9
msgid "Install Zed"
msgstr "安裝 Zed"

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:11
msgid "Zed is available on macOS, Windows, and Linux."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:13
msgid ""
"For macOS, you can download it from zed.dev/download, or install via "
"Homebrew: `brew install zed-editor/zed/zed`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:16
msgid ""
"For most Linux users, the easiest way to install Zed is through our "
"installation script: `curl -f https://zed.dev/install.sh | sh`"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:19
msgid ""
"After installation, you can launch Zed from your Applications folder (macOS) "
"or directly from the terminal (Linux) using: `zed .` This opens the current "
"directory in Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:23
msgid "Import Settings from VS Code"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:25
msgid ""
"During setup, you have the option to import key settings from VS Code. Zed "
"imports the following settings:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:27
msgid "Settings Imported from VS Code"
msgstr "從 VS Code 匯入的設定"

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:29
msgid ""
"The following VS Code settings are automatically imported when you use "
"**Import Settings from VS Code**:"
msgstr ""

