#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:250
msgid "Differences in User Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:252
msgid "No Workspace"
msgstr "無工作空間"

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:254
msgid ""
"VS Code uses a dedicated Workspace concept, with multi-root folders, `.code-"
"workspace` files, and a clear distinction between “a window” and “a "
"workspace.” Zed simplifies this model."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:257
msgid "In Zed:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:259
msgid ""
"There is no workspace file format. Opening a folder is your project context."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:261
msgid ""
"Zed does not support multi-root workspaces. You can only open one folder at "
"a time in a window."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:263
msgid ""
"Most project-level behavior is scoped to the folder you open. Search, Git "
"integration, tasks, and environment detection all treat the opened directory "
"as the project root."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:265
msgid ""
"Per-project settings are optional. You can add a `.zed/settings.json` file "
"inside a project to override global settings, but Zed does not use `.code-"
"workspace` files and won’t import them."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:267
msgid ""
"You can start from a single file or an empty window. Zed doesn’t require you "
"to open a folder to begin editing."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:269
msgid ""
"The result is a simpler model: Open a folder → work inside that folder → no "
"additional workspace layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:272
msgid "Navigating in a Project"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:274
msgid ""
"In VS Code, the standard entry point is opening a folder. From there, the "
"left-hand panel is central to navigation. Zed takes a different approach:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:277
msgid ""
"You can still open folders, but you don’t need to. Opening a single file or "
"even starting with an empty workspace is valid."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:278
msgid ""
"The Command Palette (`Cmd+Shift+P`) and File Finder (`Cmd+P`) are primary "
"navigation tools. The File Finder searches files, symbols, and commands "
"across the workspace."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:279
msgid "Instead of a persistent panel, Zed encourages you to:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:280
msgid "Fuzzy-find files by name (`Cmd+P`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:281
msgid "Jump directly to symbols (`Cmd+Shift+O`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:282
msgid ""
"Use split panes and tabs for context, rather than keeping a large file tree "
"open (though you can do this with the Project Panel if you prefer)."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:284
msgid ""
"The UI keeps auxiliary panels out of the way so navigation stays centered on "
"code."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:286
msgid "Extensions vs. Marketplace"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:288
msgid ""
"Zed does not offer as many extensions as VS Code. The available extensions "
"are focused on language support, themes, syntax highlighting, and other core "
"editing enhancements."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:290
msgid ""
"Several features that typically require extensions in VS Code are built into "
"Zed:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:292
msgid ""
"Real-time collaboration with voice and cursor sharing (no Live Share "
"required)"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:293
msgid "AI coding assistance (no Copilot extension needed)"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:294
msgid "Built-in terminal panel"
msgstr "內建的終端機面板"

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:295
msgid "Project-wide fuzzy search"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:296
msgid "Task runner with JSON config"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:297
msgid "Inline diagnostics and code actions via LSP"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:299
msgid ""
"You won’t find one-to-one replacements for every VS Code extension, "
"especially if you rely on tools for DevOps, containers, or test runners. "
"Zed's extension catalog is still growing and remains smaller."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:301
msgid "Collaboration in Zed vs. VS Code"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:303
msgid ""
"Unlike VS Code, Zed doesn’t require an extension to collaborate. It’s built "
"into the core experience."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:305
msgid "Open the Collab Panel in the left dock."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:306
msgid ""
"Create a channel and [invite your collaborators](https://zed.dev/docs/"
"collaboration#inviting-a-collaborator) to join."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:307
msgid ""
"[Share your screen or your codebase](https://zed.dev/docs/"
"collaboration#share-a-project) directly."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:309
msgid ""
"Once connected, you’ll see each other's cursors, selections, and edits in "
"real time. Voice chat is included, so you can talk as you work. There’s no "
"need for separate tools or third-party logins."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/vs-code.md:311
msgid ""
"Learn how [Zed uses Zed](https://zed.dev/blog/zed-is-our-office) to plan "
"work and collaborate."
